# Regional SEO

Check `docs/decisions/` before changing routing or SEO behaviour.

- URL segments: `au`, `uk`, `us`, `nz` (not BCP 47 in paths)
- hreflang values: `en-AU`, `en-GB`, `en-US`, `en-NZ`
- Default region: Australia (`au`)
- Use `getRelativeLocaleUrl()` / `getAbsoluteLocaleUrl()` — never hardcode `/au/`
- Trailing slashes: always (`trailingSlash: 'always'`)
- Every regional page: canonical + self-referencing hreflang + all four alternates + `x-default` → `/`
- `x-default` points to root region picker unless ADR says otherwise
